what's going on guys this is rob and we  are back today with another installment  of our series examining omega level  mutants and today  we're talking about jamie braddock also  known as monarch so jamie braddock was  created by chris claremont herb tremp  and fred creda and first debuted in  captain britain weekly number nine in  1976. now jaime's the oldest child of  the braddock family an aristocratic  family whose financial means  no longer match their social status and  the older brother of the twin siblings  brian who later became captain britain  and then betsy  better known as psylocke now in his  adulthood jaime takes control of  braddock industries and the company  thrives due to his vast financial  knowledge he's also a famous race car  driver because apparently running a  multi-billion dollar corporation was not  interesting enough on his own  you know i wonder how it is that he  became a race car  driver you know i know how he became a  race car driver he used skillshare  yes he did as you guys know i love  skillshare i absolutely love skillshare  those of you guys who don't know  skillshare is an online learning  community with thousands of aspiring  classes for creatives and curious people  you can explore new skills and develop  existing interests and  get lost in creativity what you guys may  not know is that one of my favorite  creators is a guy named thomasfrank and  thomas frank  has a skillshare program where he  basically teaches you how to be creative  and to be productive  in fact his course is actually called  productivity for creatives build a  system that brings out your best but in  all seriousness given the way the last  year  transpired i've been looking to build up  new skills and just try new things that  either i'd put on the back burner or  just never seem to get around to and now  i'm making time for me and skillshare is  a great place to learn to do that  whether you're looking to get into  photography or you want to create  youtube videos and you got to learn how  to write scripts and how to shoot your  videos and how to edit effectively  skillshare can teach you  all of that stuff and so to get you guys  started the first 1 000 people to use  the link in my description will get a  free trial of the skillshare premium  membership and after that it's only  around 10  a month so make sure you guys go check  them out and let's get back into the  video  so having said all that jamie ultimately  ends up developing a gambling problem  and basically finds himself turned into  a life of crime to pay off his gambling  debts now ultimately jaime ends up  finding himself getting kidnapped by a  guy named dr crocodile who basically  screws with his brain and jaime ends up  going crazy believing everything around  him to be a dream in addition to driving  him crazy the trauma jamie experience  also triggered his mutant powers which  normally activate in mutants during  adolescence but had remained latent in  jaime well into adulthood and it's then  that jaime discovers he has the ability  to warp reality now there are several  characters in marvel comics that can  warp reality but with monarch we  actually get an explanation of how  exactly he's  able to do this so jaime perceives  reality as a series of quantum strings  that he can manipulate tighten loosen or  untie to literally  change the fabric of reality his powers  allow him to alter the size and shape of  objects or people  and alter the memories of others he can  control any form of energy and is able  to create portals that allow him to see  things on the other side of the world or  even into other realities now monarch  has also demonstrated the ability to  increase or decrease the level of  resistance that others have to reality  warping or telepathic attacks  as he did with his sister betsy after  raising her from the dead he also has  superhuman durability and healing  making it nearly impossible to harm him  through conventional means and has even  survived being stabbed  in the head with psylocke psionic blade  without ever flinching now one of the  most impressive feats monarch has  achieved was the creation of the fury a  cybernetic construct capable of mass  destruction now jaime patterned the fury  after a being of the same name  in the parallel reality of earth 238 by  another reality warping mutant named mad  jim jaspers now jaspers created that  version of the fury to destroy all  superpowered beings on his earth except  for himself and eventually succeeded in  killing captain britain after she bailed  on that reality but the fury that jimmy  braddock created seemed to be nearly  identical to the original fury and was  able to emit  extremely powerful energy blasts  equivalent in power to a small star and  is resistant to almost  all damage now when the fury did sustain  damage it was able to restore its body  and was able to produce nanites that  could transform  any nearby technology into an extension  of itself the fury possessed super  strength with  no upper limit and was able to analyze  the abilities of its opponents and  update its defenses  accordingly it took the combined power  of rachel summers  creating a black hole with her  telekinesis and working in tandem with  storm and bishop's energy powers being  channeled into rachel through the x-men  sage who's being kept alive during the  process by drawing on wolverine's powers  to take down  the fury so yeah the fury was capable of  destroying an entire planet and monarch  was able to just  create it at will which is a testament  to his prowess as a reality warper but  perhaps the most impressive thing we've  ever seen him do  is use his reality warping abilities in  the white hot room so the white hot room  serves as the home of the phoenix force  and exists within the imcron crystal  which contains the nexus of all  realities and is the origin of all  matter that exists in all realities  within marvel comics but because it  exists outside  of reality the white hot room should be  impenetrable by reality warpers but  monarch was able to tear the fabric  comprising the room's boundary  and pull psylocke and rachel out of it  and back to their reality  so even though jamie braddock's power is  limited by his sanity  this feat suggests that he is an  extremely adept reality warper which is  why he's designated as a mega level  easily which has recently been confirmed  in jonathan hickman's definitive list of  omega level mutants but having said that  it's a pretty short video let me know  what you guys think down in the comments  and i will catch you all later peace
 

